2026-09-28 — diagnostic-option inventory, NOT closed option support

driver-diagnostic-policy.c reduces ten original musl warning categories.
The sealed GCC14 controls are compile-only, not runtime tests. With each
category's original flag, all ten reject. Without it, GCC accepts cases
2, 3, 4, 7 and 9; the rest already reject.
The exact stderr/argv are retained in diagnostics-gcc.json.

The initial EvoCC emission survey rejects cases 0 and 1, accepts cases 2..7
and 9, and reaches E3101 for case 8. Exact warning options themselves are all
explicit driver refusals, not implemented warning policies. The subsequent
return/call constraint repair corrects cases 5, 6 and 8 at the shared frontend;
return-conversion-constraints.out gives its final evidence and positive GNU
controls. This does NOT implement -Werror=pointer-sign, pointer-arith,
discarded qualifiers, or every musl diagnostic option. Do not remove approved
GNU source semantics merely to mimic a warning promoted by an unimplemented
command-line option. B08b remains open.

